Come practice your reading skills and read aloud to a friendly dog or cat -- your very own furry audience!nbsp; You can bring a book from home or borrow one from the Children's Room.nbsp; This program is perfect for emergent readers.nbsp; Children in grades K-8 are welcome to participate.nbsp;nbsp;
You may register for a 10-minute session online beginning two days before the event.nbsp;Please only reserve spots for the children participating (not adults) and provide the child's name in the registration with parents' email information
For accessibility accommodations (ex. ASL), please fill out the online form at sccld.org/accessibility 7+days prior to the event. If you need assistance with the form, speak with a staff member at your local library, call (408) 540-3945, or email us at ask@lib.sccgov.org.

Grab your guitar, grab your ukulele - let's jam! Join us every week, singing and strumming along with popular songs in a fun, easy-going environment. Meet people who are also working on their music journey, learn new chords/strums, and get encouragement to practice towards mastering your instrument. Bring your own guitar or ukulele, all other materials will be provided. Intermediate players and abovenbsp;are welcome.nbsp;
No registration, just drop in and jam. Space is limited and will benbsp;first come, first served.nbsp;**Please note that there will be no jam on November 24th.
For accessibility accommodations (ex. ASL), please fill out the online form at sccld.org/accessibility 7+days prior to the event. If you need assistance with the form, speak with a staff member at your local library, call (408) 540-3945, or email us at ask@sccl.org.

Come join us every Tuesday for Infant Toddler Storytime!
Infant Toddler Storytimenbsp;invites babies and their caregivers to learn together by strengthening their relationship with each other through stories, songs, bounces, tickles, rhymes, books, and play.nbsp;
After Storytime concludes, we invite you to Stay Play! The Storytime librarian will join in the fun with special toys, giving babies and parents time to connect.nbsp;
ADA Accommodation Requests
This program is developed to align with the Early Education Quality Standards.Free.nbsp; Attendance limits follow SJPL guidelines.

