Come practice your reading skills and read aloud one on one with a furry friend! Each 15-minute session is with a specially trained therapy dog and their volunteer.nbsp;Reading Buddies in the Gilroy Library will take place the 1st Tuesdaynbsp;of each month starting in September. Sign-ups are first come, first serve until all slots are filled.nbsp;
For children innbsp;PreK - 6th grade.
¡Ven a practicar tus habilidades de lectura y lee en voz alta uno a uno con un amigo peludo! ¡Cada sesión de 15 minutos es con un perro de terapia especialmente entrenado y su voluntario! Los "Reading Buddies" en la Biblioteca de Gilroy tendrán lugar el 1er martesnbsp;de cada mes a partir de septiembre. Las inscripciones seran por orden de llegada hasta que se llenen todos los espacios.nbsp;
Para niños desde Prekínder hasta 6to grado.

Participating in the Reading to Childrennbsp;program is a great way for children to develop their imagination and spark a love for books, reading and learning.nbsp;
Children will enjoy one-on-one or small group interaction with our volunteer. They are also welcome to practice reading to our volunteer.nbsp;Pre-registration is not required, and children may drop in to hear a story any time during the program.nbsp;
This program is best suited for preschoolers and children in grades K to3 and will be held in the Children's area.
Free. No registration required.

Storytime is a fun and interactive experience designed to accommodate a mix of ages and invites the entire family to participate in early literacy activities such as stories, songs, rhymes, fingerplays, and movement activities.nbsp; This program promotes the joys of reading and learning for children of all ages and their parents/caregivers!nbsp;
Free, with limited capacity.
Seating for Storytime is available on a first-come, first-served basis. A limited number of tickets will be distributed at the Information Desk 30 minutes prior to the start of Storytime.nbsp;
This program is developed to align with the Early Education Quality Standards.
ADA Accommodation Requests

The Cricut Open Lab is a 45-minute learning session on select Fridays with machines available to use. First-time users can learn what the Cricut machine is and how it works. You can also watch these tutorial videos ahead of time to get a better idea of how to use the Cricut machine and Design Space.nbsp;For those who already have experience using Cricut, they are welcome to register tonbsp;use a machine independently to cut out their designs. We will have Cricut machines (Explore/Air and Maker), limited supplies, and several designs available for participants.nbsp; Individuals or groups up to 3 people can register for the program.
Registration required.nbsp;Call or stop by the Vineland Library to register in advance.nbsp;
This program is generously sponsored by the Friends of the Vineland Branch Library.

Come join us at East SJ Carnegienbsp;Branch Library for our LEGO® Club! Participate in a weeklynbsp;engineering challenge or make whatever you want!nbsp;
Important: This event is recommended for children 5 and older.nbsp;Small LEGO® pieces can be choking hazards for younger children.nbsp;
No registration required.ADA Accommodation Requests

